.env
.DS_Store

# Lockfiles are intentionally NOT committed. A package-lock.json generated on one OS (e.g.
# Windows locally) records OS-specific optional-dependency bindings (native binaries for
# packages like rolldown/esbuild) that don't resolve correctly on a different OS (e.g. Render's
# Linux build environment) — a known npm bug: https://github.com/npm/cli/issues/4828. Always
# letting `npm install` resolve fresh on whichever machine is building avoids this entirely.
package-lock.json
client/package-lock.json
server/package-lock.json
